\item When $\theta$ is low..
\begin{itemize}\item Again, matters most for small grid size. And zero wrapping (which essentially makes a smaller grid than torodial wrapping. Low theta (1-2) for bigger grids is actually quite nice. Fig. \ref{fig:lowthetagrid5}, \ref{fig:theta1grid5} \end{itemize}
